  "href": "strategic_games/core/strategic_games_core_unilateral_deviation_mfogt.html",
  "body_html": "<h1>Unilateral Deviation</h1>\n<p>Given a profile $s\\in S$, a player $i$, and an alternative strategy\n$t_i\\in S_i$, the unilateral deviation of player $i$ replaces only player\n$i$'s component:\n$$\n  (t_i,s_{-i})_j=\n  \\begin{cases}\n    t_i, &amp; j=i,\\\\\n    s_j, &amp; j\\ne i.\n  \\end{cases}\n$$\nThis is the basic local move used in best-response, dominance, and Nash\nequilibrium conditions.</p>",
